messages:
emily-cs: Quick escalation — AcmePayments says our code-assist output regressed after last rollout. Generated TS misses initialization in constructor and leaves out an import. Their build now fails with TS2345.

emily-cs: Repro steps from the customer:
1) POST to /v1/code-assist with model=code-assist-v2.1, prompt attached below.
2) Receive completion, paste into project, tsc fail.

emily-cs: Prompt they used:
```
// Prompt: generate a TypeScript class for a payment client that uses axios with proper imports and initializes baseUrl and apiKey in constructor.
```

emily-cs: Expected snippet:
```ts
import axios, { AxiosInstance } from 'axios';

export class PaymentClient {
  private client: AxiosInstance;
  constructor(private baseUrl: string, private apiKey: string) {
    this.client = axios.create({ baseURL: baseUrl, headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${apiKey}` } });
  }
  // ...methods...
}
```

emily-cs: Model output they got (truncated):
```ts
// missing import for axios
export class PaymentClient {
  private client: AxiosInstance;
  constructor(baseUrl: string, apiKey: string) {
    // no initialization of this.client, uses baseUrl variable directly later -> runtime/compile errors
  }
}
```

rahul-se: Yikes. Do we know if this correlates with the v2.1 rollout earlier today? Any canary logs?

deploy-bot: Deploy notice: code-assist-v2.1 rolled to prod at 1918763000 UTC; canary 10% -> 100% at 1918763200.

emily-cs: Customer reports started failing around 1918763400. They were on hosted API (us-west). Attached request id from their call: req_0a9f2b3c.

rahul-se: Thanks. Can you paste the raw request payload (prompt + params) and the full completion text? Need to check if tokenization/truncation or a decoding bug removed initialization. Also what temperature/top_p?

emily-cs: Params: {"model":"code-assist-v2.1","temperature":0.0,"max_tokens":320,"stop":null}. Full completion attached in customer's support ticket (I copied the snippet above).

olivia-eng: Is this only missing imports/initialization or are there other structural regressions? Any tests failing besides TS compile?

emily-cs: They also reported style drift — previously we emitted explicit typed members and imports; now output uses undeclared types and references. A few other customers in our org Slack reported small diffs but not breaking. This one is a hard break for them.

mike-platform: Marking P1. Rahul, can you triage model behavior vs runtime bug? Could be altered postprocessing or a new tokenizer mapping in v2.1 that affects leading import lines (prefix trimming).

rahul-se: I'm pulling the generation logs for req_0a9f2b3c. Also checking the decode pipeline for trimming leading imports when prompt length near max_tokens. If there's a bug that chops the start of the generated output, that would explain missing imports/initialization.

rahul-se: Quick check — customer max_tokens=320, prompt length is ~280 tokens. If model returns 600 tokens but we cap to 320, we should truncate tail, not head. Investigating where head-truncation could occur.

emily-cs: Customer included their local step: they always wrap returned completion into a file and run tsc. We asked them to retry with max_tokens=800 temporarily and paste result, but they're blocked in CI until we confirm.

mike-platform: If this is rollout-related, recommend temporary mitigation: 1) Offer them to pin to previous model (code-assist-v2.0) for now. 2) Enable request-level fallback (if compile error detected, auto-call v2.0). Olivia, can you add a console toggle for immediate pin/fallback?

olivia-eng: I can add a fallback route flag in console, but need an emergency rollout approval. I'll prepare a short-run feature flag to route affected orgs to v2.0 while we debug.

rahul-se: For triage: grabbing the exact tokenization of their prompt and the raw logits/decoded tokens. Also checking commit for v2.1 that changed postprocessing (strip_prefix/strip_suffix). If anyone on infra saw a change to the response sanitizer, flag it.

emily-cs: Customer agreed to pin to v2.0 for now if we can do it quickly. They're also fine sharing the full completion and sample project privately.

mike-platform: OK. I'll coordinate with sales to offer credits and with infra to allow pin. Rahul and Olivia, keep updates here. If you want me to escalate to SRE/eng-runtime, say now.

rahul-se: I'll update within 2h with initial findings. If we find it's model output (not truncation), we'll open a regression with research and roll a fast patch to v2.1 or revert.

emily-cs: Thanks — leaving customer on the line and will update ticket with pin option. :thumbsup:

mike-platform: Noted. Logging this thread to the incident tracker as CODEGEN-REG-1918765432.
